  "slug": "fields-spatial-transcriptomics-d7eb",
  "summary": "Several new diffusion, VAE-GAN, contrastive and graph-attention frameworks target cross-modal, cross-tissue and spatial multi-omics integration and translation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is learned latent spaces that bridge modalities, tissues or spatial context. For modality translation, scPriorDiff uses network-prior-guided latent diffusion between scRNA and scATAC, and scXOrGAN maps unpaired transcriptomes between organs of one individual. BRIDGE applies contrastive learning to impute donor-specific expression across GTEx tissues. In imaging-to-expression prediction, SimpleP2G finds encoder choice (Virchow2) drives pathology-to-gene performance, and CAMEO fuses partially paired pathology and expression data. Spatial multi-omics integration uses graph-conditioned diffusion (SpatialMuSC), dual-graph attention (SPAMO) and hybrid attention for small domains (GLAND). GASTON-VI and GaLF-ST model spatial gradients and continuous expression fields. scOnion scores per-cell cross-modal concordance, and LeCellModel estimates cell typicality from latent density. Benchmarking and infrastructure appear in GNEval, which tests gene networks from 11 foundation models, and AUTOENCODIX. The new emphasis is on explicit generative or concordance-aware fusion rather than plain embedding concatenation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
